# Vernacular command

What a block of kernel vernacular is: its command, its body and its statement,
and the shape of its proof. A submission may use only the commands that add
names or ask questions; everything else the vernacular offers — notation, macros,
fixity, namespaces, sections, `Open`, `Export`, `Structure`, `Quotient`, `Opaque`,
the literate forms — changes how later text reads, so it is refused rather than
reasoned about.

## Note
Whether a block is a comment.

## To isCommentBlock (block: Text) -> Bool:
    Return startsWith(block, "--") or startsWith(block, "/-").

## Note
A block's command: its first word after the visibility words the kernel reads
past; `comment` for a comment and `literate` for the literate forms.

## To commandOf (block: Text) -> Text:
    If isCommentBlock(block):
        Return "comment".
    Let ws be words(block).
    If startsWith(block, "##") or length of ws is equal to 0:
        Return "literate".
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is less than length of ws and ["Local", "Private", "Protected"] contains item i of ws:
        Set i to i + 1.
    Let w be item i of ws.
    If w is equal to "Let" or ((w is equal to "A" or w is equal to "An") and block contains " is either"):
        Return "literate".
    Return w.

## Note
The commands a submission may use, and the fewer a statement may: a statement
asserts nothing, so it has no `Axiom` and no `Theorem`.

## To submissionCommands () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["comment", "Definition", "Theorem", "Axiom", "Inductive", "Check", "Eval", "Print"].

## To statementCommands () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["comment", "Definition", "Inductive", "Check", "Eval"].

## Note
The text after a block's first `:=`, trimmed, without its closing period.

## To bodyOf (block: Text) -> Text:
    Let parts be splitN(block, ":=", 2).
    If length of parts is less than 2:
        Return "".
    Return removeSuffix(trim(item 2 of parts), ".").

## Note
The statement between a declaration's name and its `:=`.

## To headTypeOf (block: Text) -> Text:
    Let parts be splitN(item 1 of splitN(block, ":=", 2), ":", 2).
    If length of parts is less than 2:
        Return "".
    Return trim(item 2 of parts).

## Note
The steps of a tactic script, each its first word: the SHAPE of a proof with
every name and term taken out. A proof by a term is the one step `term`.

## To tacticSkeleton (block: Text) -> Seq of Text:
    Let body be bodyOf(block).
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    If startsWith(body, "by ") is equal to false:
        Return ["term"].
    Repeat for step in split(removePrefix(body, "by "), ";"):
        If length of words(step) is greater than 0:
            Push item 1 of words(step) to out.
    Return out.

## Note
The theorem a submission must contain to prove the goal `goalName`.

## To proofNameFor (goalName: Text) -> Text:
    Return "proof_of_" + goalName.

## Test: a block's command is read past visibility words

For each of these cases:

| block                                   | command      |
|-----------------------------------------|--------------|
| "Private Definition x : Nat := Zero."   | "Definition" |
| "Local Notation \"a ++ b\" := (f a b)." | "Notation"   |
| "-- note"                               | "comment"    |
| "## Theorem: T"                         | "literate"   |
| "A Colour is either Red or Blue."       | "literate"   |
| "Print Axioms t."                       | "Print"      |

Expect that commandOf(block) is equal to command.

## Test: a theorem's statement, body and skeleton are read

Let t be "Theorem p : goal := by intro n; induction n as [ | k ih]; rfl; rw [ih]; rfl.".
Expect that headTypeOf(t) is equal to "goal".
Expect that tacticSkeleton(t) is equal to ["intro", "induction", "rfl", "rw", "rfl"].
Expect that tacticSkeleton("Theorem p : goal := fun (n : Nat) => refl Nat n.") is equal to ["term"].
Expect that proofNameFor("goal") is equal to "proof_of_goal".

## Test: names and spacing do not change a skeleton

For all booleans spaced:
    Let mutable t be "Theorem a : goal := by intro m; rfl.".
    If spaced:
        Set t to "Theorem b  :  goal :=  by intro z ;  rfl.".
    Expect that tacticSkeleton(t) is equal to ["intro", "rfl"].
